{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea","id":1170054,"title":"Advice on a PC idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-23T18:14:41-08:00","id":1170054,"title":"Advice on a PC idea","content":"I am thinking about getting M:20 for Christmas and while thinking up possible characters, this one stood out to me. His name is Basil Wittlebone, a 35 year old Security Guard and Navy Vet who is about to Awaken. Basil himself is usually a no-nonsense sort of man who uses both his military training and physical size to his advantage. Basil is usually gruff and often times, downright rude, to most people in the street. However, he is a kind, loving individual to one person, his daughter, Veronica.<br /> <br /> Basil and his daughter share a special bond due to the fact that he is a single father, having divorced with her Mother after she cheated on him. As a Mage, Basil would have to balance both his responsibilities to his Tradition, Craft or Convention and taking care of his beloved daughter. My question is how to make this PC interesting and what Tradition, Craft or Convention would really take a member who has a child?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T21:49:13-08:00","id":1170088,"title":"","content":"The PC it's already interesting, in my opinion, but it lacks a fundamental aspect of a Mage character...his approach to Magick(tm).<br /> As a Mage, you should have strong opinions about how the world works and how to make it work to your benefit. Mechanically, this will reflect on your Paradigm/Practice/Instruments .That's what makes you a mage vs an interesting dude.<br /> <br /> Mages are valuable and thus being attached with your family isn't going to ban you from any group. The Technocracy will make sure that you understand that the work comes first and family later, of course (and they have ways to ensure such loyalty).<br /> <br /> Mages are very varied, some factions may be somewhat more inclined to accept a family than others, but ultimately it isn't a heavy factor, so better think about what kind of magic you want to do, choose a number of factions that share such paradigm, and then let's see how these factions deal with family issues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:24:44-08:00","id":1170111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170088#post1170088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are valuable and thus being attached with your family isn't going to ban you from any group. The Technocracy will make sure that you understand that the work comes first and family later, of course (and they have ways to ensure such loyalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...this depends on the reading of the Technocracy you're going with. Back in Guide to the Technocracy, operatives basically HAD to abandon their Oldlife in order to serve the Union in their Newlife. If this is true, then while the Union might set up the man's daughter with everything she'd need for a comfortable life in order to ensure his eternal loyalty, he may very well be forced to take as trade that he'll never be allowed to see her again. Unless there's some reason why he was be needed in his old identity, that is (given his backstory, I doubt it).<br /> <br /> As such, if presented with the option of joining the Technocracy or another group, he would be faced with the choice of giving his daughter a good life he can never be a part of, or taking the risks of a more informal organization in return for continuing to be in her life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T05:35:16-08:00","id":1170150,"title":"","content":"I have no idea how a security guard would view the world and his approach to magic would be. Also, i am guessing that he joins the Traditions he would either join The Celestial Chorus or The Akhestic Brotherhood. The one he would not join is the Verbena due to the fact that he is scared that they might use his daughter as part of a ritual.<br /> <br /> He would probably be NWO as a Technocrat and if he joins a craft he would be be a member of The Temple of Solomon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 12-24-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T11:33:35-08:00","id":1170244,"title":"","content":"Why the Celestial Chorus or the Akashics? Is that because the image of those groups appeals to you as player? Or is there something in his background that you haven't stated that segues with monotheistic-like faith-based magic or introspection-based-East Asian-oriented/martial arts mysticism? &quot;I love my daughter&quot; seems to be the thing that defines him the most so far and that doesn't really have very much to do with magic of any sort at all. So, if the daughter is so core that she has to have something to do with his Awakening, you need a hook for that.<br /> <br /> Seems like the Chorus would be easier. Add in a religious upbrining to him. Doesn't have to be anything overwhelming. Just enough to know the fundamentals. Like, say, a Sunday/Days of Obligation-style Church of England (his name is Basil after all...) Then, hell, I dunno, his daughter gets hurt or very sick and he falls back to the only thing he's ever known that promises something miraculous and prays for her and BOOM, gets something, somehow, religious-like. And, hopefully draws the attention of a Chorister or someone who will get him to a Chorister for his Mage orientation.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you need to work on some backstory that just ain't there so far. Like his devotion to his daughter doesn't have much to do with his magic at all. Maybe he feels like he mostly abandoned her as a child while he was off a navy-ing and now he is (trying?) to make up for lost time. (Honestly, killing the mom off might be better than just a cheating spouse. Navy-man ends up getting saddled with a daughter and after the WTF! shock ends up realizing that being a dad is the most fulfilling thing possible....) Then you are going to need some hooks to the Akashics. Something that happened while he was in the navy that set him up to think of magic in Akashic terms (being present during a wu xia-style battle on the docks of Hong Kong after a night of drunken merriment) which is there in the back of his head until something happens.... there's Awakening.... Whatever. It's pretty sketchy because the connection between a doting dad security guard and what the Akashics are about is pretty tenuous with a lot more to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T12:05:26-08:00","id":1170255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170244#post1170244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the Celestial Chorus or the Akashics? Is that because the image of those groups appeals to you as player? Or is there something in his background that you haven't stated that segues with monotheistic-like faith-based magic or introspection-based-East Asian-oriented/martial arts mysticism? &quot;I love my daughter&quot; seems to be the thing that defines him the most so far and that doesn't really have very much to do with magic of any sort at all. So, if the daughter is so core that she has to have something to do with his Awakening, you need a hook for that.<br /> <br /> Seems like the Chorus would be easier. Add in a religious upbrining to him. Doesn't have to be anything overwhelming. Just enough to know the fundamentals. Like, say, a Sunday/Days of Obligation-style Church of England (his name is Basil after all...) Then, hell, I dunno, his daughter gets hurt or very sick and he falls back to the only thing he's ever known that promises something miraculous and prays for her and BOOM, gets something, somehow, religious-like. And, hopefully draws the attention of a Chorister or someone who will get him to a Chorister for his Mage orientation.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you need to work on some backstory that just ain't there so far. Like his devotion to his daughter doesn't have much to do with his magic at all. Maybe he feels like he mostly abandoned her as a child while he was off a navy-ing and now he is (trying?) to make up for lost time. (Honestly, killing the mom off might be better than just a cheating spouse. Navy-man ends up getting saddled with a daughter and after the WTF! shock ends up realizing that being a dad is the most fulfilling thing possible....) Then you are going to need some hooks to the Akashics. Something that happened while he was in the navy that set him up to think of magic in Akashic terms (being present during a wu xia-style battle on the docks of Hong Kong after a night of drunken merriment) which is there in the back of his head until something happens.... there's Awakening.... Whatever. It's pretty sketchy because the connection between a doting dad security guard and what the Akashics are about is pretty tenuous with a lot more to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose those two because those are actually my favorite two Traditions in the game, besides the Sons of Ether. I love the idea of him being a widower and trying to make up for not being there for most of her early childhood. I should work on his backstory more before trying to chose a Tradition for him to join. The Choir of course, seems to be the easiest to make work. But, others, like the Euthanatoi, i need to figure out why a former Navy Man-At-Arms would become involved with basically a death cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T12:52:34-08:00","id":1170262,"title":"","content":"Let's see, a former Navy Man-At-Arms has skills the Euthanatoi need and the wisdom and judgement to know that you sometimes have to kill someone but that killing is one of many options. As a security guard who is a veteran, he certainly can't use the force in most security operations the military would use.<br /> <br /> If Temple of Solomon is the Templars, they could work as another group. There's a 3-point Flaw in Mage 20 Book of Secrets called Ward (page 66) that would cover the complications of the daughter.<br /> <br /> If your mage is part of a cabal, what are the other players playing? It's going to be a lot easier to integrate the gruff Navy armsman and his daughter into the story if they have good ties to other characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T13:09:33-08:00","id":1170267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170262#post1170262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see, a former Navy Man-At-Arms has skills the Euthanatoi need and the wisdom and judgement to know that you sometimes have to kill someone but that killing is one of many options. As a security guard who is a veteran, he certainly can't use the force in most security operations the military would use.<br /> <br /> If Temple of Solomon is the Templars, they could work as another group. There's a 3-point Flaw in Mage 20 Book of Secrets called Ward (page 66) that would cover the complications of the daughter.<br /> <br /> If your mage is part of a cabal, what are the other players playing? It's going to be a lot easier to integrate the gruff Navy armsman and his daughter into the story if they have good ties to other characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Now that i think of it, the Euthanatoi seem to be a fitting faction for him, along with the Chorus. Now i am picturing a scene where my guy is trying to stuff a body of a dead NWO agent in his closet while trying to keep his daughter from entering the room. I wonder how my guy could've began thinking about the Cycle of death and rebirth the Euthanatoi always make a big deal about and I wonder how the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Euthanatoi </span></span></span>could've come into contact with him? Also, it is actually Master-At-Arms, not Man-At-Arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T14:45:35-08:00","id":1170283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea#post1170054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is how to make this PC interesting and what Tradition, Craft or Convention would really take a member who has a child?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Which Tradition&quot; mostly depends on the PC's approach on Magick. Does he know he's able to do Magick or he merely thinks he's doing mundane, even if well-trained, things? If his magick is Corrispondence 1 sniping, Force 2 body throws or Life 3 tsubo punching he may just be an Orphan following his own Military paradigm. So I'd define the kind of magic effects he's used too at first and maybe then decide who's going to find him first.<br /> <br /> Choristers and Templars can fit if you see him as a religious man, Euthanatoi are a good pick too but only if he can see murders as a necessity; Akashayana... could be, but then again it depends on personal philosophy because their ascetic attitude is just not for everyone; if none of the above, then the CoX can probably have him. Technocracy would probably use him in NWO or Void Engineers (depending on the campaign setting), Iteration X may be a nice third choice if you cyberize him a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T15:59:38-08:00","id":1170304,"title":"","content":"Good advice. I should determin which Sphere he is the most familiar with then chose a faction. Him being a CoX member could either be good or bad. At one hand, it could loosen him up and make less of a gruff jack-ass. But, he has a kid and coming home drunk after a Cult meeting does not sound like the best idea for a father, unless he just uses music for his Ecstasy, I could also see him being a member of the Children's Crusade, that is if it's still a thing in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T20:19:13-08:00","id":1170347,"title":"","content":"From my experiences with vets which is highly anecdotal I'm going to make these suggestions. There were some general repeats I'd say, some were particularly faithful, some very pragmatic some very disciplined etc.<br /> <br /> IF Faith is part of his lens of the world then unless he had an unusual upbringing the Chorus or the Knights Templar are really his only option. I mean it is america he could be a neopagan so Verbena could be an option(Thor's hammer is a recognized sign for military headstones!) here but Chorus is probably your go to.<br /> <br /> If he pragmatically wants to &quot;now learn magic&quot; the two Traditions that look like Magic to your average American would be the Order of Hermes and the Verbena. There's a strong faith side of the Verbena but there's also plenty of pragmatic wisewomen/men handing down their way and adapting with the times.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of tech options if he was in the Navy. I mean the &quot;i was trained to operate and maintain state of the art military technology and all it gets me is a job as a Rentacop&quot; rather writes itself. This would easily give you an inroad into The Etherites, the Adepts, or even the Technocracy, <br /> <br /> The Euthantos are odd, but since most of them require a near death experience to join its a pretty simple story there. He dies he sees the wheel, he comes back and is trained in the ways of the Euthanatos. I would point out In the game I'm currently playing in there's a euthanatos who was an army medic, so I very much see the soldier traditions of discipline and duty as tying very well with the Euthantos also in m20 they are no longer tied to Entropy alone as a favored sphere, a would be healer is very much at home among them as a would be killer. Hell maybe he has a couple of buddies who didn't come back who are doing the ghost thing.<br /> <br /> The Akashics are rather simple with the various factions built around enlightenment through martial training. Still &quot;That zen bullshit&quot; may not be the sort of place for a gruff navy man.<br /> <br /> The ecstatics well here we have another direction to go, rejection. One of my friends who is an exMarine is very much against any form of heirarchy joining wanting as much freedom as possible. I can rather see this as leading into someone on this Tradition. There's also all sorts of methods of obtaining Ecstacy that wouldn't limit yourself to music, or drugs but overall I think it would be perhaps one of the weaker fits.<br /> <br /> Finally the Dreamspeakers, generally fairly outside the bounds of most Americans in mindset, I mean he could always have been part of some culture he's rejected(Native American being teh most obvious but there's other factions) on the other hand, for many a shaman the Spirits choose them. If he can see and hear them and they make demands well there is a pragmatic need there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T20:36:15-08:00","id":1170350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170304#post1170304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good advice. I should determin which Sphere he is the most familiar with then chose a faction. Him being a CoX member could either be good or bad. At one hand, it could loosen him up and make less of a gruff jack-ass. But, he has a kid and coming home drunk after a Cult meeting does not sound like the best idea for a father, unless he just uses music for his Ecstasy, I could also see him being a member of the Children's Crusade, that is if it's still a thing in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 hasn't yet gone into the internal factions of the Traditions but I see no reason why the Children's Crusade would no longer exist. That said, nothing about the character as you've presented him, strikes me as a CoX, which the Crusade is a group within.<br /> <br /> To echo Aleph's words, you really should nail down the character's Beliefs on Magic.<br /> <br /> With what you've given, about the only groups I could see him at the top of my head is either a Syndicate Enforcer or NWO Operative. If you wish to roll Technocrat. Though I do agree with the others and their thoughts on some of the other groups.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I highly recommend picking up alongside M20 some of the Revised Edition Tradition/Convention Books. Mage is really the only of the WoD lines that I highly recommend players read the Tradition/Convention Book of the group they want to play to wrap their heads around their core beliefs and practices. You don't have to but it really helps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T20:59:21-08:00","id":1170359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170350#post1170350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 hasn't yet gone into the internal factions of the Traditions but I see no reason why the Children's Crusade would no longer exist. That said, nothing about the character as you've presented him, strikes me as a CoX, which the Crusade is a group within.<br /> <br /> To echo Aleph's words, you really should nail down the character's Beliefs on Magic.<br /> <br /> With what you've given, about the only groups I could see him at the top of my head is either a Syndicate Enforcer or NWO Operative. If you wish to roll Technocrat. Though I do agree with the others and their thoughts on some of the other groups.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, I highly recommend picking up alongside M20 some of the Revised Edition Tradition/Convention Books. Mage is really the only of the WoD lines that I highly recommend players read the Tradition/Convention Book of the group they want to play to wrap their heads around their core beliefs and practices. You don't have to but it really helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice. I might pick those up during Christmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T21:46:10-08:00","id":1170368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170359#post1170359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the advice. I might pick those up during Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div>DriveThruRPG has PDF Bundles for both groups, allowing you to buy a bunch together at a lower overall price. There's the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134717/Mage-Revised-Traditions-BUNDLE?cPath=1_6531\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Revised Traditions Bundle</a> which has the Rev Ed TBs for the Nine Traditions and the Hollow Ones and the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187968/Technocratic-Union-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Technocratic Union Bundle</a> which has the Rev Ed Convention Books, Guide to the Technocracy, the First Edition Convention Books and Technomancer's Toybook. Though I should warn you that the 1E Convention Books, like much of the 1E are kind of wonky and tends to paint them as villains despite being from their perspective. Stick to Guide and the Rev Ed for the Technocracy and how to use them in-game, read the 1E for the amusement.<br /> <br /> Of course, either bundle could be more than you are able or willing to spend, especially throwing M20 on top of it, at which I'd recommend just focusing on those groups that most interest you and getting just their splat books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T21:58:11-08:00","id":1170370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170368#post1170368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DriveThruRPG has PDF Bundles for both groups, allowing you to buy a bunch together at a lower overall price. There's the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134717/Mage-Revised-Traditions-BUNDLE?cPath=1_6531\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Revised Traditions Bundle</a> which has the Rev Ed TBs for the Nine Traditions and the Hollow Ones and the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187968/Technocratic-Union-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Technocratic Union Bundle</a> which has the Rev Ed Convention Books, Guide to the Technocracy, the First Edition Convention Books and Technomancer's Toybook. Though I should warn you that the 1E Convention Books, like much of the 1E are kind of wonky and tends to paint them as villains despite being from their perspective. Stick to Guide and the Rev Ed for the Technocracy and how to use them in-game, read the 1E for the amusement.<br /> <br /> Of course, either bundle could be more than you are able or willing to spend, especially throwing M20 on top of it, at which I'd recommend just focusing on those groups that most interest you and getting just their splat books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might buy the books for The Celestial Chrous, Eunthantos, Etherites and either the Verbena or Dreamspeakers. Besides his views on magic the big seller for him, at least ICly, is how the Tradition he plans on joining reacts to the fact he has a kid. Because, he would never abandon her or let her be used by anyone, even his own master. In fact, he might respond with aggression if someone even hints something bad about his daughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T22:23:11-08:00","id":1170375,"title":"","content":"If you want the 1e books, The Traditions Gathered are the volumes collecting various traditions. Traditions Gathered 3 would get you the Chorus and Euthantos and Akashic Brotherhood. Traditions Gathered 2 has the Cult of Ecstasy, Verbana and Dreamspeakers. Traditions Gathered 1 has the Order of Hermes, Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts.<br /> <br /> Also, given how M20 works on paradigm, an Orphan is a much more viable option. You have a specialty sphere of your choice and could make the practices similar to a preferred Tradition but have a character who is not a joiner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T22:46:43-08:00","id":1170377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170350#post1170350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With what you've given, about the only groups I could see him at the top of my head is either a Syndicate Enforcer or NWO Operative. If you wish to roll Technocrat. Though I do agree with the others and their thoughts on some of the other groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Void Engineer, they have both naval assets and a friggen space navy. The &quot;go out and protect the world from Alien Horrors&quot; is a pretty easy sell for a navy guy with a daughter.<br /> <br /> Iteration X is also really big on producing military hardware, sure he wouldn't be machine cult side of things but they do need people who can do tests in the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T01:56:10-08:00","id":1170387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170370#post1170370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, he would never abandon her or let her be used by anyone, even his own master. In fact, he might respond with aggression if someone even hints something bad about his daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember though that the Awakening sets the mages apart from common people. His daughter is bound to grow distand and beeventually estranged because she will naturally feel that his father is now &quot;different&quot;, maybe even creepy... it's not a relationship that's going to last, or at very least to last happily. Older Tradition mages surely knows that, while the Technocracy is probably going to manipulate them into splitting &quot;for her own safety&quot; (remember Man in Black?).<br /> <br /> Also: it's not like the Technocracy is going to ask much. If they find him first they'll ask, then move to capture and brainwash should the answer be no. Eventually he'll agree to their terms and share their vision of necessity, maybe dreaming about the day he'll finally be able to retire and live with her daugther again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 12-25-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T04:52:08-08:00","id":1170405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170387#post1170387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just remember though that the Awakening sets the mages apart from common people. His daughter is bound to grow distand and beeventually estranged because she will naturally feel that his father is now &quot;different&quot;, maybe even creepy... it's not a relationship that's going to last, or at very least to last happily. Older Tradition mages surely knows that, while the Technocracy is probably going to manipulate them into splitting &quot;for her own safety&quot; (remember Man in Black?).<br /> <br /> Also: it's not like the Technocracy is going to ask much. If they find him first they'll ask, then move to capture and brainwash should the answer be no. Eventually he'll agree to their terms and share their vision of necessity, maybe dreaming about the day he'll finally be able to retire and live with her daugther again.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat could be a good source of drama when then eventually begins to happen. The daughter now is 12 and is starting middle school. I can see the relationship starting as fine but as the months and years go by she starts to grow more and more distant, eventually moving out the first chance she gets. This, of course would probably leave my guy devastated since, well, she is the only family he has left. That is, if the Technocrats don't get him first. If they do, they will probably separate them &quot; for her own good&quot; and while my guy is going NWO or Void Engineer, he will be thinking about his daughter and possibly watching her from the distance, watching her grew up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T07:26:11-08:00","id":1170420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170370#post1170370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might buy the books for The Celestial Chrous, Eunthantos, Etherites and either the Verbena or Dreamspeakers. Besides his views on magic the big seller for him, at least ICly, is how the Tradition he plans on joining reacts to the fact he has a kid. Because, he would never abandon her or let her be used by anyone, even his own master. In fact, he might respond with aggression if someone even hints something bad about his daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is, in the beginning of MtAs, like VtM and WtA, there was very much a 'You can't go home again' vibe, that while Mages may be the most human of the Big Five splats, they're still ultimately Other like the rest. Over time that got dialed back a bit but it's still very much an up in the air thing. And honestly I think that's because most people aren't going to create PC's that haven't left their former friends and family for the wonders of the Awakened life. For instance, in M20 Book of Secrets which has the previously mentioned Ward flaw, has other family-related merits and flaws. It even has a section on child mages. But the first story in the M20 anthology revolve around an initiate in the Order of Hermes that has recently not just given up her old name, past and family but the OoH subjected her and her fellow initiates to a procedure to change their faces.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge and memory, there aren't Traditions that deal with the family members of mages like you're looking for. Like I said, the general assumption seems to be that the Mage will largely leave them behind for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> That said, this strikes me as something determinant by the Storyteller and in turn the local leaders of said Mage group(s).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170377#post1170377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Void Engineer, they have both naval assets and a friggen space navy. The &quot;go out and protect the world from Alien Horrors&quot; is a pretty easy sell for a navy guy with a daughter.<br /> <br /> Iteration X is also really big on producing military hardware, sure he wouldn't be machine cult side of things but they do need people who can do tests in the field.</div> </div> </div> </div>The VE is a possibility, especially if its Rev Ed VE who have been largely forced back to Earth, become incredibly militant and hardened by everything, and locked in a dangerous, covert war with Threat Null.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that reminds me, all the Rev Ed books are set after an event known as the Avatar Storm (or the Dimensional Anomaly to the Technocracy) which did a number on the Mages, their leadership and their beyond Earth holdings. M20 goes into this, provides options and how to handle it all.<br /> <br /> As for ItX, they could work as well and again, especially in the Rev Ed where events have cause them to change and clean up their act.<br /> <br /> Though I still see the character more as a NWO Operative and a Syndicate Enforcer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T10:41:29-08:00","id":1170475,"title":"","content":"If i chose not to do this PC, i have been thinking up a secondary PC that might be interesting too. I already came up with a backstory up to the point where he about to Awaken. If i tell you it, can you guys give me your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T10:44:05-08:00","id":1170476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170475#post1170475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i chose not to do this PC, i have been thinking up a secondary PC that might be interesting too. I already came up with a backstory up to the point where he about to Awaken. If i tell you it, can you guys give me your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T10:59:00-08:00","id":1170483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170420#post1170420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To my knowledge and memory, there aren't Traditions that deal with the family members of mages like you're looking for. Like I said, the general assumption seems to be that the Mage will largely leave them behind for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> That said, this strikes me as something determinant by the Storyteller and in turn the local leaders of said Mage group(s).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm of a special lineage&quot; is a suggested Paradigm as of M20, I would imagine there are those among the Verbena and Etherites who'd specificially be focused on family to an almost eugencist level. Chorus would probably vary I mean some would push the monastic life but there's plenty of &quot;keep your ties to your family&quot; faiths. I'd imagine the Order of HEmes is probably the MOST likely to be &quot;you are a member of the Order first, your old life is gone&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T11:52:13-08:00","id":1170497,"title":"","content":"Here is the backstory for my second PC idea.<br /> <br /> Big Tom Miller always thought of himself as life's punching bag. Born to drug addicts, Tom and his older brother Rice, were often neglected by their parents, who were too busy trying to get their next high to be worried about their sons. When Tom was three, he and Rice were taken away and put in separate foster homes. Tom unfortunately, had even more bad luck when every single foster family he was placed in turned out to be worse then his original parent's. By the time Tom was 16, he turned to wrestling for his school's team in order to vent his frustrations. He proved natural at this and even managed to please his latest foster father, who, though not abusive, wanted his foster son to be tough.<br /> <br /> Tom became so embroiled with his physical accomplishments that he neglected his academic career. He eventually dropped out of school and was immediatley kicked out by his foster father, who had recently adopted him, saying he did not want a deadbeat dropout living with him. Tom, who immediatley realized his grave mistake, turned to crime in order to support himself and found, that he was a natural leg-breaker. Tom then spent the next 12 years in his life working for various criminals as hired muscle, occasionally finding himself in and out of prison a lot. When he was 30, Tom was nearly killed after a drug deal went bad, but somehow miraculously survived a gunshot wound to the chest.<br /> <br /> Tom, who was tossed into jail yet again, realized that if he kept up his criminal behavior, he would be dead sooner or later. During his latest jail sentence, he was deep in a excistential crisis about his life so far and how pointless it all seemed. Recently however, he seemed to get a new fixation on life and after gaining parole, immediatley disappeared from the public eye, causing his old criminal accomplices and his parole officer to wonder what the &quot; Big Lug&quot;, as they affectionatly called him, was up too.<br /> <br /> My idea for this character is that he either met someone in Prison who introduced him to the concept of magic or he decided to try out the mystical arts as a way to give his life meaning again. What do you guys think of this PC? Also, i will give a list of possible traditions that he would join up with and tell why through the words of Tom himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T12:51:16-08:00","id":1170508,"title":"","content":"He has a practically Stereotypical Euthantos story right there. Nearly died, takes a new turn. Akashic would also be a a good fit, there's a strong mythic resonence there of finding redemption in the Monestary(or similar sects). The Chorus or Verbena would also be pretty solid on the &quot;Finding God&quot; as might to a lesser Extent Dreamspeakers. The Ecstatic experience practically writes itself.<br /> <br /> The Ones I'd imagine would be a hard push would be Adepts, Etherites and the Order of Hermes. Even then I can see &quot;guy gets into wierd tech/computers&quot; in prison and breaks out/awakens. So really the order would be the hardest one to setup.<br /> <br /> If you're going Technocracy Syndicate is probably easiest one to work with followed by the NWO. Though really &quot;Prison experiment awakens&quot; is a pretty easy to way to get into the Progenitors or IX.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T13:20:46-08:00","id":1170519,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions so far. The big problem with Tom, besides having a parole officer on his back, is the fact that he is not very smart. If you want his exact IQ, he has the same IQ Forrest Gump had. If he goes Technocrat, they may need to find a way to &quot;fix&quot; his IQ, unless the Syndicate or NWO don't mind having a slightly stupid leg-breaker working for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T15:03:49-08:00","id":1170531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170519#post1170519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the suggestions so far. The big problem with Tom, besides having a parole officer on his back, is the fact that he is not very smart. If you want his exact IQ, he has the same IQ Forrest Gump had. If he goes Technocrat, they may need to find a way to &quot;fix&quot; his IQ, unless the Syndicate or NWO don't mind having a slightly stupid leg-breaker working for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flowers_for_Algernon\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flowers_for_Algernon</a> Easily something that Either Technos or Trads could do for him. A progenitor prison experiment on a mentally challenged individual that awakens is and gives them both enlightenment and a higher IQ practically writes itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T17:41:33-08:00","id":1170560,"title":"","content":"That could be a actual thing i can use if i go Technocrat. Also, here is his reasons for joining either The Akashics or The Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> With the Akashics, Tom shared a cell with a Asian-American who happened to be a nearly Awakened student of the Akashics. Tom eventually grew curious about why his cell mate was doing stuff like meditation and practically fasting every week. Of course, Tom got curious and asked his cell-mate, whom he was friends with, why he was doing it. Then The Cell-Mate went into a ramble about Inner-Peace, Martial Arts and concepts Tom could not comprehend. After having it explanied in simple terms, Tom actually grew interested in what his cell-mate was talking about and asked him where he could learn it too. That either leads him to skip out on parole and head to a monastery in Asia or find a Akashic master in America.<br /> <br /> The Dreamspeakers have a some-what similar reason. In this one, Tom grew extremely sick and had to go to the infirmary. Then, a Dreamspeaker posing as a Shamanic healer arrived a few weeks later to heal a Native American inmate. Tom, being desperate, asked the Shaman to heal him too and, to his surprise, he agreed. A day after the ritual, Tom felt better and was convinced that it was the Shaman who healed him. During the rest of his time in prison, he researched everything he could about Shamanism and after getting parole, set out to find the Healer to ask him to teach him his ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T18:33:13-08:00","id":1170567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170560#post1170560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be a actual thing i can use if i go Technocrat. Also, here is his reasons for joining either The Akashics or The Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> With the Akashics, Tom shared a cell with a Asian-American who happened to be a nearly Awakened student of the Akashics. Tom eventually grew curious about why his cell mate was doing stuff like meditation and practically fasting every week. Of course, Tom got curious and asked his cell-mate, whom he was friends with, why he was doing it. Then The Cell-Mate went into a ramble about Inner-Peace, Martial Arts and concepts Tom could not comprehend. After having it explanied in simple terms, Tom actually grew interested in what his cell-mate was talking about and asked him where he could learn it too. That either leads him to skip out on parole and head to a monastery in Asia or find a Akashic master in America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of Akashic teachers in America, hell there's a whole faction built around Western Martial arts if you want to go abit wierd. I'll just point out though with Mind its pretty damned easy to buff ones Mentals as it were so improving your mind would be something they could do easily long term or even to the self.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dreamspeakers have a some-what similar reason. In this one, Tom grew extremely sick and had to go to the infirmary. Then, a Dreamspeaker posing as a Shamanic healer arrived a few weeks later to heal a Native American inmate. Tom, being desperate, asked the Shaman to heal him too and, to his surprise, he agreed. A day after the ritual, Tom felt better and was convinced that it was the Shaman who healed him. During the rest of his time in prison, he researched everything he could about Shamanism and after getting parole, set out to find the Healer to ask him to teach him his ways. </div> </div> </div>Dreamspeakers are have alot of options, I'd personally have a spirit take interest in Tom. A Dreamspeaker might not care about teaching some random white guy orphan but having a spirit make an argument for him well....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T18:44:04-08:00","id":1170569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170567#post1170567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plenty of Akashic teachers in America, hell there's a whole faction built around Western Martial arts if you want to go abit wierd. I'll just point out though with Mind its pretty damned easy to buff ones Mentals as it were so improving your mind would be something they could do easily long term or even to the self.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers are have alot of options, I'd personally have a spirit take interest in Tom. A Dreamspeaker might not care about teaching some random white guy orphan but having a spirit make an argument for him well....</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what spirit would take a interest in a Forrest Gump-like ex-con?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T20:29:01-08:00","id":1170582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170054-advice-on-a-pc-idea?p=1170569#post1170569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what spirit would take a interest in a Forrest Gump-like ex-con?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many kinds of spirits could. It depends on how you want to handle them coming together and their relationship. Hell, the 'spirit' could in fact be his Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T08:57:55-08:00","id":1170695,"title":"","content":"I am picturing the spirit and him having a conversation on a bus on the way to where the Dreamspeaker who healed him lives, with the other passengers looking at the idiot talking to himself. The spirit in question could very will be his avatar. I am also picturing it being either a Lune or some kind of water spirit.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}